From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: sfp: add TP-LINK SM410U fixed 2500BASE-X quirk

The TL-SM410U exposes no PHY over I2C. Use the fixed 2500BASE-X host
interface from the MediaTek reference quirk. Its advertised 1G/2.5G
copper rates do not establish SGMII support on the serial host side.
The SGMII-only trial did not link with a 1G copper peer on RE-CS-08.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -611,6 +611,10 @@ static const struct sfp_quirk sfp_quirks
 	SFP_QUIRK_F("Turris", "RTSFP-10G", sfp_fixup_rollball),
 
 	SFP_QUIRK_S("ZOERAX", "SFP-2.5G-T", sfp_quirk_oem_2_5g),
+	/* Copper line rates are internal to the module; its known host
+	 * interface is fixed 2500BASE-X, with no PHY accessible over I2C.
+	 */
+	SFP_QUIRK_S("TP-LINK", "TL-SM410U", sfp_quirk_oem_2_5g),
 };
 
 static size_t sfp_strlen(const char *str, size_t maxlen)
